# App wording

User-facing strings (teacher, popups, buttons, empty states, coach chat) should read like something you would say out loud.

## Do not use dashes as punctuation

Do not use `—`, `–`, or a spaced hyphen (` - `) to join clauses. It looks generated.

```
Hold E and F# as crotchets — each gets a full beat.
Pitch looks settled — colour on the score.
```

```
Hold E and F# as crotchets so each gets a full beat
1 note sat outside pitch
```

Ranges in UI copy use words (`Bar 1 to 2`), not `Bar 1–2`.

Hyphens inside words and note names stay (`F#`, `in-tune` in code only).

## No full stop on short tips

Popup lines, chips, and bullet/dot points do not end with `.`

Normal sentences in a longer teacher reply may use full stops. Short clipped tips do not.

## Bullets vs one line

Use two short bullet points when there is both “what happened” and “what to try”, or when several notes in one highlight share the same fix.

Keep a single line when one short sentence is enough, for example starting with the beat.